            <div id="service-overview">
                <h3 class="govuk-heading-l">Service overview</h3>
                <p class="govuk-label">The View Your Payments service allows you to:</p>
                <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
                    <li>View a list of all payments received from the DfE for the last 3 years.</li>
                    <li>Filter your view of these payments by a selected date range.</li>
                    <li>
                        View a breakdown of each bank payment by transaction description and print or export this information.
                    </li>
                    <li>Filter and view transactions using a selected date range and export this information.</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
            <div id="payment-history-view">
                <h3 class="govuk-heading-l">Your payment history view</h3>
                <span class="govuk-label">This page shows all of the payments made into your bank account from the DfE within the date range shown in the date selection filter.  You are able to view up to three years’ worth of payments from this page</span>
                <div class="help-page-content-payment-summary"><img src="../images/PaymentSummary.png" /></div>

                <p class="govuk-label">This page contains the following key features:</p>
                <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--number">
                    <li><b>Date range filters</b>: Use these filters to display DfE payments from your own custom date range. Type in the desired date range of the payments you would like to view (from and then to) and then press the Apply button for these results. The Reset button will clear your custom date range and return to the default, which shows the most recent payments for the last 180 days.</li>
                    <li><b>Payment date and amount</b>:  This is a list of all your payments from the DfE with the most recent first. The date indicates when the funds were transferred into your bank account. You can view up to three years’ worth of payment history by adjusting the date filters above this list.</li>
                    <li><b>View payment details</b>: Use this link to access your ‘remittance’ view, this shows a more detailed breakdown of individual transactions for each payment. For more information, please go to Your payment details view.</li>
                </ul>

            </div>
            <div id="payment-details-view">
                <h3 class="govuk-heading-l">Your payment details view</h3>
                <span class="govuk-label">This page is your ‘remittance’ from the DfE.  It shows a detailed breakdown of the individual payments that were made to your organisation’s bank account. This view includes buttons to Download as CSV or Download to PDF.</span>
                <div class="help-page-content-payment-details"><img src="../images/PaymentDetail.png" /></div>
                <p class="govuk-label">Each transaction row is made up of the following data columns:</p>
                <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--number">
                    <li><b>Date</b>: the bank transfer payment date for these funds.</li>
                    <li><b>Contract number</b>: the unique reference number for the contract reference that this transaction belongs to. You will find this in the Summary of Funding and Funding Agreements section of your contract documents.  More information on individual allocations can be found on your Allocation statements page.</li>
                    <li><b>Budget group</b>: the budget group that this transaction has been assigned to. For more information, read Your budget groups.</li>
                    <li>
                        <b>Description</b>: the detailed explanation of what this transaction is for. Where applicable the funding description follows a standardised order to show:
                        <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
                            <li>The age-band of learners that the payment is for.</li>
                            <li>The name of the funding stream.</li>
                            <li>The type of transaction. For example, capping, profile or reconciliation (see further notes on transaction types below for a full explanation of these terms).</li>
                        </ul>
                    </li>
                    <li><b>Amount</b>: the exact sum of money that has been paid to you for this transaction.</li>
                </ul>
                <div id="transaction-capping">
                    <p><b>Further notes on transaction types:</b></p>
                    <h4 class="govuk-heading-s">Capping</h4>
                    <p>Funding paid on actual delivery is capped to the maximum value of the funding stated in your contract for a given period or ‘financial envelope’.  The most common period is financial year, i.e. August to March as one financial envelope and April to July as another financial envelope. There is no funding flexibility across financial envelopes so under-delivery in one period cannot be used to fund over-delivery in another period.</p>
                    <p>Capping is re-assessed after each ILR data submission, to take account of any changes to your contract value, actual delivery and/or DfE policy.  To achieve this, the payments are calculated in two steps: </p>
                    <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
                        <li>
                            Payments are calculated based on your latest ILR data submission, bringing payments to-date in line with your actual delivery, and thus reversing out any previous capping values.
                        </li>
                        <li>capping is then calculated afresh based on the latest data you have provided.</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
                <div id="transaction-profile">
                    <h4 class="govuk-heading-s">Profile</h4>
                    <p>Where the term ‘Profile’ is shown next to a transaction this indicates that payment has been made based on the monthly delivery profile in your contract.</p>
                </div>
                <div id="transaction-reconciliation">
                    <h4 class="govuk-heading-s">Reconciliation</h4>
                    <p>Where the term ‘Reconciliation’ is shown next to a transaction this indicates that payment has been made based on the actual delivery data you have submitted in the ILR.  This can also apply to transactions that have been generated due to a funding claim reconciliation (if any of the funding you receive is subject to funding claims).  Funding claim reconciliation transactions usually appear on your remittances in December and/or January.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
