            <div id="payment-transaction-view">
                <h3 class="govuk-heading-l">Your filter and export transactions view</h3>
                <span class="govuk-label">This page allows you to filter, view and export your detailed payment transactions for a custom date range shown in the date selection filter. You are able to view and export up to three years’ worth of transactions from this page. This view includes a button to download the transactions as a CSV file.</span>
                <div class="help-page-content-payment-transaction"><img src="../images/PaymentTransactions.png" /></div>
                <p class="govuk-label">This page contains the following key features:</p>
                <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--number">
                    <li><b>Date range filters</b>: Use these filters to display transactions from your own custom date range. Type in the desired date range of the transactions you would like to view (from and then to) and then press the Apply button to display these results. The Reset button will clear your custom date range and return to the default, which shows the most recent transactions for the last 30 days.</li>
                    <li><b>Transaction description filters    </b>: Use this filter to display specific transactions from the set date range. Click inside the search box to show a drop down of all your available transaction descriptions or type the first few letters of the transaction description that you wish to search for. Click on an item in the drop down list to make a selection and add to the filter box. To remove the item simply click the ‘X’ in the blue box. Once all selections have been made press the Apply button to display these results. Note- selected transactions items will not display if this data does not exist for the date range that has been set.</li>
                    <li><b>Budget group summary section</b>:  This section shows a total of all payments received for the selected date range. Click the ‘+’ to expand the summary and display totals for each Budget group for the transactions in the selected date range.</li>

                    <p class="govuk-label">Each transaction row is made up of the following data columns:</p>

                    <li><b>Date</b>: the bank transfer payment date for these funds.</li>
                    <li><b>Contract number</b>: the unique reference number for the contract reference that this transaction belongs to. You will find this in the Summary of Funding and Funding Agreements section of your contract documents. More information on individual allocations can be found on your Allocation statements page. </li>
                    <li><b>Budget group</b>: the budget group that this transaction has been assigned to. For more information, read Your budget groups.</li>
                    <li>
                        <b>Description</b>: the detailed explanation of what this transaction is for. Where applicable the funding description follows a standardised order to show:
                        <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
                            <li> The age-band of learners that the payment is for.</li>
                            <li> The name of the funding stream.</li>
                            <li> The type of transaction. For example, capping, profile or reconciliation (see further notes on transaction types below for a full explanation of these terms).</li>
                        </ul>
                    </li>
                    <li><b>Amount</b>: the exact sum of money that has been paid to you for this transaction.</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
